INFO  [Claude Code] I've successfully resolved the issue preventing test creation for `MarketDataProcessor.<init>`. The problem was a `NullPointerException` in the `DisplayFormat` constructor at line 35.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Root cause:** When Diffblue Cover tried to construct a `MarketDataProcessor` instance, it attempted to create a `DisplayFormat` listener with a null `Instruments` parameter. The constructor immediately tried to call methods on the null object (`instruments.getPriceWidth()` and `instruments.getSizeWidth()`), causing a `NullPointerException`.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] **Solution implemented:** Added defensive null checks in the `DisplayFormat` class:
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. In the constructor (DisplayFormat.java:35-38) - returns early if `instruments` is null, setting `placeholder` to an empty string
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. In the `update` method (DisplayFormat.java:69-70) - returns early if `instruments` is null
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. In the `trade` method (DisplayFormat.java:114-115) - returns early if `instruments` is null
INFO  [Claude Code] 
